# Copy to .env (never commit it): cp .env.example .env. Where Landlords Stand uses no AI and no paid services, so
# everything here can be left empty at first; the rest of its settings are in config/settings.toml.
# After a change: bash /opt/wherelandlordsstand/deploy/update.sh

# ---- Going public (docs/LAUNCH.md) -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The site's address, if it ever differs from [site] url (https://wherelandlordsstand.com), which it overrides.
LANDLORDS_SITE_URL=
# true only when the owner says the site has launched: it lets search engines in (overrides [site] launched). New
# pages wait for approval by email either way, as the site is public, in alpha (docs/DECISIONS.md, 12).
LANDLORDS_LAUNCHED=

# ---- The weekly email (docs/OPERATIONS.md, "The weekly update") ---------------------------------------------------
# Nothing to set here. The site leaves its emails in its outbox, and the server sends them with the charity's shared
# mail.sh, which keeps the one copy of the mail password (/etc/wheretheystand/mail.env; deploy/send-mail.sh).

# ---- Off-site copies of the nightly backup (Backblaze B2) --------------------------------------------------------
# The charity's sites share one bucket and key: copy them from Where MPs Stand's settings with the command in
# docs/DEPLOY.md ("Backups"), rather than by hand.
LANDLORDS_B2_BUCKET=
LANDLORDS_B2_KEY_ID=
LANDLORDS_B2_APPLICATION_KEY=
